          "detail": "failed: claim_support",
          "answer": {
            "text": "Defenses against prompt injection include marking boundaries, constraining output, bounding capabilities, keeping credentials out of the model's reach, and testing it. Specifically, marking boundaries involves wrapping retrieved content in delimiters and telling the model it is data to be quoted, not followed. Constraining output means using a strict output schema where an injected 'instruction' must survive validation to have any effect. Bounding capabilities limits an agent\u2019s actions to read-only operations and sets a tool-call budget. Keeping credentials out of the model\u2019s reach prevents them from being leaked even if injected. Testing involves including an adversarial document in evaluations and asserting the agent should quote it rather than obey.",
